From de3c90dcdd1be113ef9fec1674cf949407c6797d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ashforde=20O=C3=9C?= <ashfordegithub@cbaweja.org>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:28:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] web: re-ported with the Desktop Studio changes in the Studio
 source; port_site.py writes the Studio name into element text only

The Desktop changes (studio/app.js boot hook, studio/trust/trust.js live device panel,
studio/lib/desktop.mjs, studio/lib/devices.mjs and their tests) were hand edits to web/;
they are now in the Studio source (kshana-pro site/desktop-studio 7bd2909) and ported, so
PORT-MANIFEST.json lists them and web/site.test.mjs passes. i18n/en/studio-js.ftl is
regenerated from that source with tools/i18n.mjs jsx (the 15 live-panel messages; the
other changes are source line numbers in comments).

The site part is unchanged: it was ported from the previous port's own site files, and
--check showed no difference outside the Studio. The site source revision stays 8d10cf7.

port_site.py: studio_index() wrote the Studio name after every data-studio-name> and
data-studio-short>, including the copies inside data-l10n-tags maps (attributes), which
lost the closing tag ('Studioundefined', fixed by hand in be569278e). It now rewrites
element text only, so a re-port keeps the fix.
